@native
@label "Element of"
@description "Test membership — `needle` is in `haystack` when haystack is a string containing the needle's JS string conversion as a substring (`contains`; as `toString needle` except that null and undefined convert to \"null\" and \"undefined\", never \"\"), or a list containing a structurally equal element (equivalent to `includes haystack needle` under stock equality: NaN never found, closures by identity); any other haystack is False. This fixed bootstrap leaf does not follow reader equality overrides. The compiled parser and resolver owners retain it as a host leaf over their verified string/finite-number domain."
@tags "list" "string" "predicate"
elem : (needle: a) -> (haystack: b) -> Boolean

@native
@label "Equals"
@description "Check equality (==). numeric-tower Phase 5 (D6): the declared type is the POLYMORPHIC Eq-method shape `t -> t -> Boolean`, NOT the anomalous String-only `(a:String)->(b:String)->Boolean` (it was always used generically; the JS impl is loose `==`). This native is the global total-Boolean FAST PATH; the principled API is the `Eq.eq : a -> a -> Maybe Bool` class method (per-rung instances in dispatch-instances.fenel). Behaviour unchanged — the String `Eq` IS the lexical compare (the LLVM `llvmHasStringTypedArg` String-escape keys on call-site arg types, not this decl, and stays); the DirectOp `F64Eq`/`oeq` lowering keys on the fnId, not this decl."
@tags "comparison"
eq : (a: t) -> (b: t) -> Boolean

@native
@label "Exact value equality"
@description "Decide whether two values are the same value with the engine's exact value equality (the owner that decides enum membership): Just true or Just false when it decides, Nothing when it cannot (unreadable, host-shaped or oversized data, an undecided numeric owner). Records and variants compare field by field; callables compare by identity; $ref handles compare as their handle text; NaN is never equal. ∀a. a → a → Maybe Bool"
@tags "comparison"
exactValueEqual : (left: a) -> (right: a) -> Maybe Bool

@native
@label "F32 → 4 bytes (little-endian)"
@description "Encode a Number as the 4-byte little-endian byte sequence of its IEEE 754 single-precision representation (each byte 0–255). Mirrors the `new Float32Array([n]) → new Uint8Array(buffer)` round-trip on a little-endian host. The primitive byte-iteration surface for binary serializers — e.g. Wasm's `f32.const` operand encoding."
@tags "binary" "codec" "ieee754"
float32ToBytesLE : (n: Number) -> List Number

@native
@label "F64 → 8 bytes (little-endian)"
@description "Encode an IEEE 754 double as its 8-byte little-endian byte sequence (each byte 0–255). Mirrors the `new Float64Array([n]) → new Uint8Array(buffer)` round-trip on a little-endian host. The primitive byte-iteration surface for binary serializers — e.g. Wasm's `f64.const` operand encoding."
@tags "binary" "codec" "ieee754"
float64ToBytesLE : (n: Number) -> List Number

